      "writtenOn": "2022-06-17T16:17:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As per my understanding, As long as there is an extra refcount on the page, or the page_ext being accessed in the path where the final put_page() happens, it will be fine. Because extra ref_count makes the offline to wait till the refcount is zero or in the final put_page() where page_ext access happens(say for page_owner) before it is freed to buddy. \n\nWith simple grep, I feel that all paths are seems fine(unless I am really missing something here), but one where the reading of /proc/page_owner information directly and there is a parallel offlining happening.\n\n/proc/page_owner                  offline\n----------------               ------------\nPageBuddy(page) returns\nfalse\n                              Frees the page to buddy\n                              and successively free the\n                              ms-\u003epage_ext\nAccess the page_ext\n\nI think there should be extra refcount of the page should be taken here.\n\nBTW, for the use case you have mentioned, page_is_idle() is just a page-\u003eflags check for 64bit. It is for 32 bit where we do page_ext-\u003eflags but memory hotplug is not enabled for 32bit systems,(If I am not wrong here), to online/offline memory blocks.",
      "parentUuid": "8169d5d6_b9fca3da",
      "revId": "05c63911b098b1d5d8f2305c36b44096575aa398",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
